Third-party software
--------------------

icedLiquid installs these packages from npm (see package.json). Each keeps
its own license; none of their code is copied into this repository.

  onnxruntime-web           MIT          (Microsoft)
  next                      MIT
  react, react-dom          MIT
  next-intl                 MIT
  next-themes               MIT
  @base-ui/react            MIT
  @huggingface/jinja        MIT
  @huggingface/tokenizers   Apache-2.0
  class-variance-authority  Apache-2.0
  clsx                      MIT
  lucide-react              ISC
  streamdown                Apache-2.0
  tailwind-merge            MIT
  tailwindcss               MIT
  zod                       MIT
  server-only               MIT

`pnpm dev` and `pnpm build` copy the onnxruntime-web runtime files (.wasm,
.mjs) into public/ort/. That folder is git-ignored and is not distributed with
the source.

The fonts Urbanist, Inter and JetBrains Mono are loaded through next/font
from Google Fonts at build time. They are licensed under the SIL Open Font
License 1.1.

The tools of the voice agent call these services from your server at run
time: WeatherAPI.com, Exa and OpenRouter (only when you set their key), and
the keyless Open-Meteo geocoding and forecast APIs (place names for the
weather tool, and the weather demo mode when no weather key is set). Their
terms of service apply to your use of them.


